 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How's life treating you? Use small, open bins with lids that slide rather than lift. Hang them above your kitchen, so you see them at eye level. As far as you can, a bit of distance. Bears don't like to run in broad daylight. Stop cooking, get inside, and don't leave food out overnight. Take down any loose food before you leave camp, so there's nothing for them to smell. It' mostly about being thoughtful. Bears are just trying to survive, but they can be unpredictable around food.",
